# Keeps the Docker build context small and, more importantly, keeps
# host-built artifacts out of the containers — e.g. frontend/Dockerfile
# does `COPY frontend/ .` after installing node_modules *inside* the
# Linux build stage; without this, a local `npm install` done on the
# host (Windows/macOS binaries for swc/esbuild) would get copied over
# and silently break the container's build.

# Python
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.venv/
**/*.egg-info/

# Node
**/node_modules/
**/.next/

# Local trace data / demo agent output
*.db
*.db-journal
demo-agent/output/

# VCS / editor
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
